Package: wickrabacktest
Type: Package
Title: Wickra Backtest Engine (R Binding)
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("kingchenc", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "support@wickra.org")
Description: R binding for the wickra-backtest engine. It calls the engine's
    stable C ABI from compiled C glue via .Call, returning the backtest report
    as a JSON string that is byte-identical to the Rust, Python, Node.js, WASM,
    C#, Java and Go bindings.
License: MIT + file LICENSE | Apache License 2.0
Suggests: jsonlite
URL: https://github.com/wickra-lib/wickra-backtest, https://backtest.wickra.org,
    https://wickra-lib.r-universe.dev
BugReports: https://github.com/wickra-lib/wickra-backtest/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
NeedsCompilation: yes
SystemRequirements: the wickra-backtest C ABI shared library. `configure`
    downloads the prebuilt library for this package's Version from the project's
    GitHub releases and bundles it, so an ordinary install needs nothing extra.
    To build against a local checkout instead, set WKBT_INC to bindings/c/include
    and WKBT_LIB to the directory holding a library you built yourself with
    `cargo build -p wickra-backtest-c --release`.
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
